(LIB-50 through LIB-52 -- mangling. Every exported function mangles to
 flat `<library>_<version>_<func>`, every component sanitized by mapping
 characters outside [A-Za-z0-9_] to _, and a leading-digit prefix applies
 only to the library component since it begins the symbol. A bare
 identifier cannot start with a digit (`Library 123kit ...` fails to
 parse as a name at all -- it lexes as an integer literal), so this uses
 the single-quoted spelling `'123kit'`, which is legal, to reach the
 leading-digit case at all: sanitizing "123kit" leaves it unchanged, but
 since it opens the mangled symbol it gets an underscore prefix. Version
 "2.0" sanitizes to "2_0" with no such prefix, since it is interior, not
 the symbol's first component. Function name "foo-bar!" sanitizes both
 punctuation characters to underscores.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox
   docs/ledger/probes/libraries/shared/LIB-mangling.vox --shared -o mangling.so
   nm -D --defined-only mangling.so
 expected output: exit 0, and:
   0000000000000396 T _123kit_2_0_foo_bar_
 (the address column is whatever this build happens to lay out; only the
 symbol name is the claim under test)
)

Library '123kit' version "2.0".

To 'foo-bar!'.
  Print "hi".
